    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48089" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thămyras</span></b> , ae,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Thracian poet</i>
			
			<i>who entered into a contest with the Muses</i>, <i>and</i>, <i>being vanquished</i>, <i>was deprived of his eyes</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 2,
			22</span></i> (3, 15), 19; <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 3, 7, 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. A. 3,
				399</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ib. 274</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 56,
				57, § 204</span></i>.—Called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thămyris</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 4,
				183</span></i>.</div>
